# Vulnerabilities in packages VENDORED INSIDE setuptools (setuptools/_vendor/).
#
# These cannot be fixed by bumping our own dependencies. Our direct pins are
# already clean: wheel 0.47.0 and setuptools 79.0.1 both scan with zero
# findings. What Trivy flags is the older copies setuptools bundles internally.
#
# The only way to replace them is to upgrade setuptools past 79.0.1, and that is
# pinned for a hard runtime reason documented in requirements.txt: setuptools
# 80.x removes the pkg_resources shim, Python 3.12 removed pkg_resources from
# the standard library, and fyers_apiv3's WebSocket client imports it. Upgrading
# breaks the market data feed outright.
#
# Reachability: these vendored modules are setuptools' own build-time machinery.
# The trading runtime never imports jaraco.context or wheel, and the exploit
# paths are archive extraction and package-index traversal, neither of which the
# bot performs. Re-evaluate whenever fyers_apiv3 stops depending on
# pkg_resources; at that point the setuptools pin can be lifted and this file
# deleted.
#
# Reviewed: 2026-08-08
CVE-2026-23949   # jaraco.context 5.3.0, vendored in setuptools
CVE-2026-24049   # wheel 0.45.1, vendored in setuptools
CVE-2025-47273   # setuptools 70.3.0, vendored copy


# ── Advisories the broker SDK's exact pins make unfixable ────────────────────
#
# fyers_apiv3 declares its dependencies with == rather than >=:
#   requests==2.31.0   aiohttp==3.9.3   protobuf==5.29.3   websocket-client==1.6.1
#
# Asking for a patched aiohttp or protobuf makes requirements.txt unsatisfiable
# against every published fyers release - pip returns ResolutionImpossible, not
# a warning. There is no version of the SDK that permits the fixed versions, so
# this cannot be resolved on our side at all until the vendor relaxes the pins.
#
# Reachability, assessed rather than assumed:
#   - The aiohttp advisories are server-side: malformed POST parsing and a
#     zip bomb through auto_decompress. Nothing here runs an aiohttp server;
#     it is a client against Fyers and Telegram.
#   - The protobuf advisories are unbounded recursion while parsing untrusted
#     messages. The only protobuf this process decodes arrives over an
#     authenticated Fyers market data socket.
#
# Revisit whenever fyers_apiv3 publishes a release with relaxed pins.
# Reviewed: 2026-08-08
CVE-2024-30251   # aiohttp 3.9.3, pinned by fyers_apiv3
CVE-2025-69223   # aiohttp 3.9.3, pinned by fyers_apiv3
CVE-2026-69244   # aiohttp 3.9.3, pinned by fyers_apiv3
CVE-2025-4565    # protobuf 5.29.3, pinned by fyers_apiv3
CVE-2026-0994    # protobuf 5.29.3, pinned by fyers_apiv3
